00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:05.430 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  as the pandemic drags on people around  the world are bracing for  still more months stuck at home until a  vaccine goes  into widespread use but in japan people  are going to great lengths to get out of  the house and as lucy craft reports from  tokyo  for some remote workers the sky  is the limit working from home  month after month can give you a bad  case of cabin fever  but now japan has found the antidote to  workplace monotony  getting taken for a ride on a ferris  wheel  converted to airborne office cubicles  yomiuri land amusement  park outside tokyo now rents office  space with the ultimate stunning views  free wi-fi but laptop and office water  cooler  not included spokesman yoo okutani said  lots of users told us the time just flew  by  18 buys you a lounge chair poolside  and one hour in rotation up to 500 feet  in the air  among the 150 takers so far were seiji  acai and his wife the online events  manager boarded a cabin for his first  gravity-defying conference call  my coworkers said it looked like i was  on vacation they were jealous he said  the amusement park has dozens of rides  but very few needless to say  are suited to desk work the roller  coaster and merry-go-round aren't laptop  friendly the spokesman said  we advise customers to ride these when  they take a break from work  meanwhile japan has thousands of cheap  rent-by-the-hour karaoke rooms  these days they're being repurposed at a  big  echo karaoke outlet in downtown tokyo  demand is growing not from  warblers but from white collar workers  meeting in this super ventilated karaoke  room instead of a coffee shop  these workers said there was just one  drawback  when we file our expense report it's  going to look like we were loafing said  this employee  and whenever work gets too intense you  can always pick up a microphone  and belt out some tunes for cbs this  morning saturday  lucy craft tokyo

